 "summary": "The assumptions sit at the natural level: the map needs no freeness, contractibility, injectivity or surjectivity, chain equivariance is stated for monoids, and the `Group` hypotheses come from Mathlib's `HomologicalComplex.coinvariantsTensorObj` (Basic.lean:79). The classifying-space square is a one-line specialization of the general quotient-cover naturality theorem, so no proof is duplicated, and limiting it to trivial coefficients matches the trivial-coefficient chain iso it builds on; local coefficients are separate future work in roadmap item 17.",
